Q: Invoking tar.exe from PowerShell, can&#39;t input any more commands A: <p>There seem to be a confusion here, your file isn't a tarball, it'd have the <code>.tar.gz</code> or <code>.tgz</code> extension otherwise. This is just a single file gzip compressed, so you can use the <code>GZipStream</code> class to expand it:</p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>Add-Type -AssemblyName System.IO.Compression
$uri = 'https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc-4.6.4/libstdc++/libstdc++-manual.pdf.gz'

try {
    $req = Invoke-WebRequest $uri -UseBasicParsing
    $gz = [System.IO.Compression.GZipStream]::new(
        $req.RawContentStream,
        [System.IO.Compression.CompressionMode]::Decompress)

    # this should be changed for the destination of the expanded archive
    # currently it will be a file with this name to the current location
    $file = New-Item libstdc++-manual.pdf -ItemType File
    $fs = $file.OpenWrite()
    $gz.CopyTo($fs)
}
finally {
    if ($gz) { $gz.Dispose() }
    if ($fs) { $fs.Dispose() }
}

Invoke-Item $file.FullName # Should open the pdf
</code></pre>
